                            Preamble

    The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for
    software and other kinds of works, specifically designed to ensure
    cooperation with the community in the case of network server software.

    The GNU General Public License is designed to make sure that you have
    the freedom to share and change all versions of a program--to make sure
    it remains free software for all its users. Many computer programs are
    designed to communicate with users over a network. The GPL permits
    programmers to make a modified version and run it on a server without
    ever releasing the source code to the public.

    The GNU Affero General Public License is designed to ensure that, in
    such cases, the modified source code becomes available to the users of
    the network service. The precise terms and conditions for copying,
    distribution and modification follow.

