    6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

    You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms of
    sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
    Complete Corresponding Source in a machine-readable format, along with
    or in a medium customarily used for software interchange, for a price no
    more than your reasonable cost of physically performing this conveying
    of source, or for no charge, if you distribute the object code by
    downloading from a network server. Or you may offer to provide this, in
    accord with subsection 6b.

    A Corresponding Source need not include anything that users can
    regenerate automatically from other parts of the Corresponding Source.

    If you convey an object code work under section 6, you can also choose
    to use a network server to provide access to the Corresponding Source.
    To do this, you must:

    a) Place the Corresponding Source on a network server accessible to the
    public without charge for the duration of at least three years starting
    from the time when you ceased distribution of the object code, or for
    as long as you offer support or warranty service for that object code,
    whichever is longer.
    b) Ensure that the Corresponding Source is available via a Standard
    Interface, and that it is easy to find at the stated network address.
    c) Ensure that all users who receive the object code are notified that
    they can retrieve the Corresponding Source from the network server.

